# Built platform artifacts. Rebuilt by `make platform-sync` in about a second, so committing
# them would version build output — which this project has already paid for once, by committing
# generated data until a repo could no longer be pushed. What IS committed is platform.lock,
# which records the platform commit a demo or a published figure was produced against.
vendor/

# The FOLIO ontology. #49 removed the hierarchy it fed; nothing has read this file since,
# and it is 17 MB copied into every image by `COPY data/ ./data/`. The industry crosswalk that
# replaced it is data/mappings/sic_to_folio.csv, which is 12 KB, checked in on purpose, and
# auditable a row at a time. Attribution stays in docs/provenance.md.
data/folio/
